// @@@ if the index is between 0 and the size of the vector inclusive, then for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the vector, the element at the next position is either null if the original element at this position was null, or it equals the original element at this position.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to the size of the vector, then for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the vector, the element at each subsequent position is either null if the old element at that position was null, or equal to the old element at that position.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to the size of the vector, then for every valid index i from the insertion point to the old size of the vector, the element at position i+1 in the updated vector should be null if the old element at position i was null, or should be equal to the old element at position i otherwise.
--------------------
